Opsec is short for Operational security.
It is the process of identifying operational critical information that may be the target of adverseries in order to disrupt your operations.
The goal is to secure the information to prevent an adversary from obtaining it. In terms of anonymity this can be used to protect and secure the information 
adversaries may use to deanonymize you.

Threat Modeling
Threat modeling is the process of getting to know your adversary, identifying information or attack vectors the adversary may exploit and then finding a way to mitigate
those exploits the adversaries may use. When these information are compiled together, it is called a threat model.
You can also use other more structured thread models such as STRIDE, CIA Triad, Attack Tress.

Stride
The stride threating model was developed by Microsoft and can be applied to almost everything. STRIDE stands for spoofing, tampering, repudiation, information disclosure
denial of service, escalate of privileges.

